These files (`promogen2_library.npz`, `promogen2_rs241.npz`) are frozen
embeddings extracted by running the `jinyuan22/promogen2-base` model
(CC-BY-NC-4.0) on CROSSHOST's regulatory sequence library. Quarantined
here, separate from the MIT-licensed core benchmark, because they are a
direct output of a non-commercially-licensed model.

**Non-commercial use only.** Commercial use requires clarifying terms with
the PromoGen2 model authors, not with the CROSSHOST project — we are not in
a position to grant rights we do not hold. See
https://huggingface.co/jinyuan22/promogen2-base for the model's own license.

DNABERT-2 embeddings (`data/core/` is NOT where these live — see
README.md's licensing quarantine table) are believed permissively licensed
(Apache 2.0-style) but this was NOT independently re-verified during Gate 8
packaging — confirm before treating them as unrestricted. See KNOWN_ISSUES.md.
